+# NIST's 2007 drawing count and the later release: a count-level lead
+
+November 14, 2026 UTC · STL02–STL03 / B188 / H005. A NIST presentation gives an exact **2,565** count for acquired shop drawings. A separately archived 2011-release mirror has **2,565 TIFF files**. The matching numbers are a lead for tracing provenance, not proof that the presentation and mirror contain the same drawings. [NIST presentation, physical slide 5](https://www.nist.gov/system/files/documents/2017/04/28/WTC7_Approach_Summary_18Dec07-Final.pdf#page=5) · [Prior mirror and release-account review](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/4057193d/investigation/broader-evidence/steel-frankel-release-accounts-2026-11-10/README.md)
+
+## Observations preserved by source
+
+| Source | Count and scope |
+| --- | --- |
+| **December 18, 2007 NIST presentation**, title slide and slide 5 | NIST describes **2,565 acquired shop drawings** and reports extensive connection-detail revisions in the ANSYS and LS-DYNA structural models. The slide also separately mentions review of **80 additional boxes** of modification and inspection documents. The page supplies no itemized list, source, date of acquisition or drawing-format breakdown. [Slides 1 and 5](https://www.nist.gov/system/files/documents/2017/04/28/WTC7_Approach_Summary_18Dec07-Final.pdf#page=5) |
+| **NIST FY 2007 annual report**, p. 2 | NIST reports acquiring shop drawings in **spring 2007** and revising connection details after review. This passage does not give a count or establish an item-level join to the presentation or to a later release. [Prior acquisition chronology](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/05fd083f14961f8c26113da181ca2669597e4de1/investigation/broader-evidence/steel-nist-source-chronology-2026-11-14/README.md) |
+| **2011 release mirror ZIP central directory**, examined suffix | This preserved directory lists **2,565 TIFF files**, **22 PDF files**, one PNG and nine directories. The TIFF count is based on filename extensions, not drawing content. The archive is a public mirror, not the original four disks or their native manifest. [Mirror](https://archive.org/download/911datasets/NIST_WTC7_FOIA_12-009.zip) |
+| **2012 requester account**, release paragraph | The account describes **42 TIFF erection sheets**, **2,523 TIFF fabrication sheets** and **22 PDF erection sheets** among **2,587 files**. These are its reported categories, not classifications independently verified for every file in the mirror. [2012 account](https://www1.ae911truth.org/en/ptv-faqs/611-wtc-7-blueprints-exposed-via-foia-request.html) |
+
+## Comparison and limits
+
+The reproduction confirms **42 + 2,523 = 2,565** and **2,565 + 22 = 2,587**. The NIST slide calls its count shop drawings; the later account distinguishes erection and fabrication sheets. The mirror count identifies TIFF extensions only. These are distinct observations with different category labels and units; keep them side by side. A broad use of “shop drawings,” overlapping categories, differing sets or a numerical coincidence are untested possibilities. No source inspected here supplies the mapping needed to choose among them.
+
+The count match does not establish inclusion of any particular sheet, identity or completeness of the 2007 set, or what NIST possessed in 2011. The independently preserved **2001–2999** account, mirror's **2001–3000** numeric-filename gap, and conflicting later statements about completeness remain unresolved. The 80 boxes are a separate reported population and should not be added to the drawing total. Nothing in these counts establishes deliberate withholding, specimen identity, or a change in the historical collapse explanation.
+
+## Next discriminating records
+
